---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Food Cost Percentage Calculator — Check a dish in 15 seconds | Main Street Toolbox"
  description="One question: is this dish priced right? Enter plate cost and menu price, get the food cost percentage, the verdict against the 28–35% band, and the price that fixes it."
  path="/restaurant/food-cost-percentage-calculator/"
>
  <div class="industry-hero">
    <div class="industry-hero-bg" style="background-image:linear-gradient(rgba(250,247,240,.82), rgba(250,247,240,.06)), url('/images/restaurant.jpg')"></div>
    <div class="container head">
    <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/restaurant">Restaurant</a> / <b style="color:var(--ink)">Food Cost %</b></p>
    <h1>Is this dish priced right?</h1>
    <p class="sub">Two numbers in, one honest answer out — in 15 seconds.</p>
  </div>

  </div>

  <main class="container check">
    <div class="pair">
      <div class="in">
        <label for="cost">Plate costs you</label>
        <div class="box"><span>$</span><input id="cost" type="text" inputmode="decimal" value="4.90" /></div>
      </div>
      <div class="in">
        <label for="price">You charge</label>
        <div class="box"><span>$</span><input id="price" type="text" inputmode="decimal" value="16.95" /></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="answer" data-level="ok" aria-live="polite">
      <div class="pct" id="fc">28.9%</div>
      <div class="word" id="word">healthy</div>
    </div>

    <div class="band">
      <div class="band-scale">
        <div class="zone"></div>
        <div class="pin" id="pin"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="band-labels"><span>15%</span><span>band 28–35%</span><span>50%</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="fix" id="fix"></div>
  </main>

  <section class="container prose">
    <h2>What the answer means</h2>
    <h3>What is a healthy food cost percentage?</h3>
    <p>Food cost percentage is the share of the menu price that goes to ingredients. Across full-service
    restaurants the healthy band is <b>28–35%</b> — the number this checker grades against. The band shifts a
    few points by concept: quick-service kitchens run leaner because portioning is mechanical and throughput is
    high, while fine dining accepts more ingredient cost against premium prices. Rezku's 2026 benchmarks:</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Concept</th><th>Typical food cost (2026)</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Coffee shop</td><td>22 – 28%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Quick service (QSR)</td><td>25 – 30%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Fast casual</td><td>28 – 32%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Casual / full-service dining</td><td>28 – 35%</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Fine dining</td><td>30 – 35%+</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <h3>Why does food cost creep up?</h3>
    <p>Almost never one big thing. It is portion drift (the 6 oz pour becoming 7 oz), supplier price creep that
    no one repriced against, and waste that never got measured. A number that climbs week over week is a portion
    or supplier problem wearing a disguise — the fix is measurement, not guesswork: cost the top sellers on the
    <a href="/restaurant/recipe-cost-calculator/">Recipe Cost Calculator</a> and see which dish moved.</p>
    <h3>How do I bring a high number down?</h3>
    <p>Price first, portion second. When the verdict above reads "tight" or "danger", the fix line shows the
    menu price that brings this dish back inside the band at a 30% target — raise that number before touching
    the recipe, because guests notice a shrinking plate faster than a dollar on the menu. If the price cannot
    move (the market will not bear it), then re-plate: a cheaper cut, a different starch, one less component.
    Change the price, watch the band, decide.</p>
    <h3>Is a dish check enough?</h3>
    <p>It is one of two rhythms. This page catches recipe problems one dish at a time; a weekly
    COGS-to-sales percentage catches theft, waste and supplier creep across the whole kitchen. Run both: check
    the top ten dishes when the weekly number moves, and re-rank the whole menu with the
    <a href="/restaurant/menu-engineering-matrix/">Menu Engineering Matrix</a> once a quarter — Stars to protect,
    Plowhorses to reprice, Dogs to retire.</p>
    <h2>Related tools</h2>
    <p>Cost the whole recipe: <a href="/restaurant/recipe-cost-calculator/">Recipe Cost Calculator</a>. Setting a
    new price from scratch: <a href="/restaurant/menu-pricing-calculator/">Menu Pricing Calculator</a>. Checking
    the whole menu at once: <a href="/restaurant/menu-engineering-matrix/">Menu
    Engineering Matrix</a>. Printing the result: <a href="/menu-maker/">Menu Maker</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="container faq">
    <h2>Questions owners ask</h2>
    <details><summary>How do I calculate food cost percentage?</summary><p>Divide what the plate costs you by what you charge, times 100. A dish costing $4.90 that sells for $16.95 has a food cost of about 29%.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Is there a free food cost calculator app?</summary><p>You do not need one — this calculator runs in the browser on any phone or tablet: nothing to download, no account, no subscription. It loads fast enough to check a price mid-service, and you can add it to your home screen like an app.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Is lower food cost always better?</summary><p>Not always. Chasing 20% by shrinking portions can hurt reviews and repeat visits. A stable 30% with strong sales beats a wobbly 24% with unhappy guests.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Should I use weekly COGS instead of a single dish?</summary><p>Both views matter. Single-dish checks catch recipe problems; a weekly COGS-to-sales percentage catches theft, waste and supplier creep. This calculator handles the dish view.</p></details>
  </section>

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    mainEntity: [
      { '@type': 'Question', name: 'How do I calculate food cost percentage?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Divide what the plate costs you by what you charge, times 100. A dish costing $4.90 that sells for $16.95 has a food cost of about 29%.' } },
      { '@type': 'Question', name: 'Is there a free food cost calculator app?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'You do not need one — this calculator runs in the browser on any phone or tablet: nothing to download, no account, no subscription.' } },
      { '@type': 'Question', name: 'Is lower food cost always better?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Not always. Chasing 20% by shrinking portions can hurt reviews and repeat visits. A stable 30% with strong sales beats a wobbly 24% with unhappy guests.' } },
      { '@type': 'Question', name: 'Should I use weekly COGS instead of a single dish?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Both views matter. Single-dish checks catch recipe problems; a weekly COGS-to-sales percentage catches theft, waste and supplier creep.' } },
    ],
  })} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebApplication',
    name: 'Food Cost Percentage Calculator',
    url: new URL('/restaurant/food-cost-percentage-calculator/', Astro.site).toString(),
    applicationCategory: 'FinanceApplication',
    operatingSystem: 'Any',
    offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
  })} />

  <style is:global>
    .head { padding: 36px 24px 8px; }
    .head h1 { font-size: var(--fs-800); margin-bottom: 6px; }
    .head .sub { color: var(--ink-2); }
    .check { max-width: 640px; padding-bottom: 32px; }
    .pair { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 14px; margin-top: 18px; }
    .in { min-width: 0; }
    .in label { display: block; font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 7px; }
    .in .box {
      display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 2px; border: 2px solid var(--line-2);
      border-radius: var(--r-m); background: var(--card); padding: 2px 14px; min-width: 0;
    }
    .in .box:focus-within { border-color: var(--green); box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px var(--green-tint); }
    .in .box span { font: 640 1.5rem var(--font-display); color: var(--ink-3); }
    .in .box input {
      flex: 1; min-width: 0; border: 0; outline: 0; background: none;
      font: 640 1.9rem var(--font-display); color: var(--ink); padding: 8px 0;
      font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    }
    .answer {
      margin-top: 22px; border-radius: var(--r-l); padding: 26px 24px; text-align: center;
      background: var(--ok-tint); border: 1px solid var(--ok);
    }
    .answer[data-level="ok"]   { background: var(--ok-tint); border-color: var(--ok); }
    .answer[data-level="warn"] { background: var(--warn-tint); border-color: var(--warn); }
    .answer[data-level="bad"]  { background: var(--bad-tint); border-color: var(--bad); }
    .answer .pct { font: 640 4.2rem/1 var(--font-display); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
    .answer[data-level="ok"] .pct { color: var(--ok); }
    .answer[data-level="warn"] .pct { color: var(--warn); }
    .answer[data-level="bad"] .pct { color: var(--bad); }
    .answer .word { font: 600 15px "Inter"; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; margin-top: 8px; color: var(--ink-2); }
    .band { margin-top: 18px; }
    .band-scale { position: relative; height: 12px; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--bad-tint); }
    .band-scale .zone { position: absolute; top: 0; bottom: 0; left: 37.1%; width: 20%; background: var(--ok-tint); border-inline: 1px solid var(--ok); }
    .band-scale .pin { position: absolute; top: -4px; bottom: -4px; width: 4px; border-radius: 2px; background: var(--ink); transition: left .18s ease; }
    .band-labels { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font-size: 12px; color: var(--ink-3); margin-top: 6px; }
    .fix {
      margin-top: 16px; padding: 12px 16px; border-radius: var(--r-s); font-size: 14.5px;
      background: var(--paper-2); border: 1px dashed var(--line-2); color: var(--ink-2); min-height: 20px;
    }
    .fix b { color: var(--ink); }
    @media (max-width: 480px) { .pair { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); } }
  </style>

  <script>
    import { beaconUse } from '../../scripts/stats';

    const costEl = document.getElementById('cost') as HTMLInputElement;
    const priceEl = document.getElementById('price') as HTMLInputElement;
    const num = (v: string) => { const n = parseFloat(v.replace(/[^0-9.]/g, '')); return Number.isFinite(n) ? n : 0; };
    // 首次改动记一次使用（每会话），与工具页 runtime 语义一致
    let counted = false;
    const countUse = () => { if (!counted) { counted = true; beaconUse('food-cost-percentage-calculator'); } };

    function calc() {
      const cost = num(costEl.value), price = num(priceEl.value);
      const fc = price > 0 ? (cost / price) * 100 : 0;
      const box = document.querySelector('.answer') as HTMLElement;
      const pct = document.getElementById('fc')!;
      const word = document.getElementById('word')!;
      const pin = document.getElementById('pin')!;
      const fix = document.getElementById('fix')!;

      if (price <= 0 || cost <= 0) {
        box.dataset.level = 'ok'; pct.textContent = '—'; word.textContent = 'enter both numbers';
        pin.style.left = '0%'; fix.textContent = '';
        return;
      }
      pct.textContent = fc.toFixed(1) + '%';
      const pos = Math.min(100, Math.max(0, ((fc - 15) / 35) * 100));
      pin.style.left = `calc(${pos}% - 2px)`;

      let level: string, wordTxt: string, fixHtml: string;
      if (fc <= 35) { level = 'ok'; wordTxt = fc < 20 ? 'very low — check the plate matches' : 'healthy'; fixHtml = 'Inside the 28–35% band full-service restaurants run at.'; }
      else if (fc <= 40) { level = 'warn'; wordTxt = 'tight'; fixHtml = `Above the 35% ceiling. Priced at <b>$${(cost / 0.30).toFixed(2).replace(/\.00$/, '')}</b> this dish returns to a 30% food cost.`; }
      else { level = 'bad'; wordTxt = 'danger'; fixHtml = `Ingredients eat ${fc.toFixed(0)}¢ of every dollar. You need about <b>$${(cost / 0.30).toFixed(2)}</b> for a 30% food cost — or re-plate this dish.`; }
      box.dataset.level = level; word.textContent = wordTxt; fix.innerHTML = fixHtml;
    }
    [costEl, priceEl].forEach((el) => el.addEventListener('input', () => { countUse(); calc(); }));
    calc();
  </script>
</BaseLayout>
